(76209, 2632, 1808, '<td valign="top">Nice implied movement and I like that it takes a few seconds to figure out what is going on.</td>', 'Nice implied movement and I like that it takes a few seconds to figure out what is going on.', '2002-06-28 22:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(76210, 2632, 1054, '<td valign="top">Simple and effective.</td>', 'Simple and effective.', '2002-06-29 21:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(76211, 2632, 1078, '<td valign="top">I''m probably giving this a higher score than everybody else, but I don''t care.  I like the color and the abstact nature of the shot -- even though it''s a very concrete (no pun intended) visual of city growth.  My only concern is all the compression artifacts, particularly around the rebar.  It may not be possible, but saving this as a less compressed .jpg might smooth all that out.  (I notice that its file size is only about 1/3 of what it''s allowed to be -- use that extra and elminate the compression.)  :-)</td>', 'I''m probably giving this a higher score than everybody else, but I don''t care.  I like the color and the abstact nature of the shot -- even though it''s a very concrete (no pun intended) visual of city growth.  My only concern is all the compression artifacts, particularly around the rebar.  It may not be possible, but saving this as a less compressed .jpg might smooth all that out.  (I notice that its file size is only about 1/3 of what it''s allowed to be -- use that extra and elminate the compression.)  :-)', '2002-06-30 16:35:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(76212, 2632, 1, '<td valign="top">Nicely composed and framed.</td>', 'Nicely composed and framed.', '2002-06-30 23:12:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(76213, 2632, 705, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone, for your comments.  Some answers:<br/>*the sky is unnaturally blue, yes.  my Kodak DX3900 seems to do this.  I don''t know why, but I usually like it, even if it''s innacurate.<br/>*''the life'', I s''pose, is implied.  I guess all this building is a side-effect of our life.<br/>Patella, thanks for the advice.<br/>Spiderman, heh, I''ll be happy to see how you use it.</td>', 'Thanks everyone, for your comments.  Some answers:*the sky is unnaturally blue, yes.  my Kodak DX3900 seems to do this.  I don''t know why, but I usually like it, even if it''s innacurate.*''the life'', I s''pose, is implied.  I guess all this building is a side-effect of our life.Patella, thanks for the advice.Spiderman, heh, I''ll be happy to see how you use it.', '2002-07-01 02:37:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(76214, 2633, 2334, '<td valign="top">heh, the roadside florist and a car parked where it''s not supposed to be...funny.</td>', 'heh, the roadside florist and a car parked where it''s not supposed to be...funny.', '2002-06-24 01:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(76215, 2633, 327, '<td valign="top">I often wonder if these guys or gals are all over the world? I''ve seen them in every city I''ve ever visited. Great shot, little too busy with so much in the background/foreground. Kee</td>', 'I often wonder if these guys or gals are all over the world? I''ve seen them in every city I''ve ever visited. Great shot, little too busy with so much in the background/foreground. Kee', '2002-06-24 13:58:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(76216, 2633, 2337, '<td valign="top">The man''s face is too shadowed.  Fill flash would have helped (although I know that''s not always possible)</td>', 'The man''s face is too shadowed.  Fill flash would have helped (although I know that''s not always possible)', '2002-06-24 16:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
