(77587, 2718, 1005, '<td valign="top">Funky hydrant, very nicely done.  Was there something ugly at the top of the building?  (A. Retentive comment about cropping, aka NIT)  Vivid colors!  <br/>Photo 9 City 8 total 8</td>', 'Funky hydrant, very nicely done.  Was there something ugly at the top of the building?  (A. Retentive comment about cropping, aka NIT)  Vivid colors!  Photo 9 City 8 total 8', '2002-06-27 21:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(77588, 2718, 2321, '<td valign="top">awsome awsome awsome!, great colors, and view!</td>', 'awsome awsome awsome!, great colors, and view!', '2002-06-28 01:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(77589, 2718, 772, '<td valign="top">very nice shot and great depth of field :)  I wonder if it would have been possible to get the top of the building in the image?  Good work! = 9 - jmsetzler</td>', 'very nice shot and great depth of field :)  I wonder if it would have been possible to get the top of the building in the image?  Good work! = 9 - jmsetzler', '2002-06-28 12:41:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(77590, 2718, 1808, '<td valign="top">Interesting point of view!</td>', 'Interesting point of view!', '2002-06-28 23:07:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(77591, 2718, 637, '<td valign="top">great perspective 6 sjgleah</td>', 'great perspective 6 sjgleah', '2002-06-29 11:35:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(77592, 2718, 1054, '<td valign="top">I love the shot, and the title.</td>', 'I love the shot, and the title.', '2002-06-30 13:51:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(77593, 2718, 1078, '<td valign="top">Really great colors.  I wish you could get the building staright to the frame, but know you can''t do so perfectly -- however, it still appears that ther photo has been rotated clockwise a bit.  You may not be able to get the side of the building to be vertical, but you can get the building to fall along the horizontal plane.  I think it needs to be rotated a little counter-clockwise.  Like how the cloud reflections in the building look like they''re logical extensions of the clouds behind it.  Good shot.</td>', 'Really great colors.  I wish you could get the building staright to the frame, but know you can''t do so perfectly -- however, it still appears that ther photo has been rotated clockwise a bit.  You may not be able to get the side of the building to be vertical, but you can get the building to fall along the horizontal plane.  I think it needs to be rotated a little counter-clockwise.  Like how the cloud reflections in the building look like they''re logical extensions of the clouds behind it.  Good shot.', '2002-06-30 19:54:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(77594, 2718, 811, '<td valign="top">Good use of color and depth.</td>', 'Good use of color and depth.', '2002-06-30 20:29:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(77595, 2718, 1, '<td valign="top">Great contrast of color AND size.  The reflections are a great touch.</td>', 'Great contrast of color AND size.  The reflections are a great touch.', '2002-06-30 23:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(77596, 2718, 1779, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for they''re comments! Regarding the building and how it seems like it''s falling... I couldn''t do anything about it, the street its not completely horizontal, so it was the hydrant or the building; and sorry I couldn''t get the hole building, it was to tall and I was already on the floor...  : (<br/><br/>LM</td>', 'Thanks everyone for they''re comments! Regarding the building and how it seems like it''s falling... I couldn''t do anything about it, the street its not completely horizontal, so it was the hydrant or the building; and sorry I couldn''t get the hole building, it was to tall and I was already on the floor...  : (LM', '2002-07-01 12:35:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(77597, 2719, 92, '<td valign="top">great angle and colors !</td>', 'great angle and colors !', '2002-06-24 01:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(77598, 2719, 1907, '<td valign="top">the photo would have been brilliant were it not for the graininess</td>', 'the photo would have been brilliant were it not for the graininess', '2002-06-24 05:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
