(78369, 2759, 2337, '<td valign="top">The line at the top took something away from the shot.  A closer crop might help.</td>', 'The line at the top took something away from the shot.  A closer crop might help.', '2002-06-25 10:24:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78370, 2759, 2351, '<td valign="top">Maybe just a little tired.....Not what I expected from your Title.</td>', 'Maybe just a little tired.....Not what I expected from your Title.', '2002-06-25 20:54:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78371, 2759, 806, '<td valign="top">Good composition and texture.</td>', 'Good composition and texture.', '2002-06-25 23:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78372, 2759, 772, '<td valign="top">lol... that''s the ''cleanest'' drunk i have ever seen :)  I think this is a neat shot... good work! = 7 - jmsetzler</td>', 'lol... that''s the ''cleanest'' drunk i have ever seen :)  I think this is a neat shot... good work! = 7 - jmsetzler', '2002-06-26 12:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78373, 2759, 1897, '<td valign="top">this looks posed, he is way to clean.</td>', 'this looks posed, he is way to clean.', '2002-06-26 18:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78374, 2759, 2314, '<td valign="top">this looks posed.</td>', 'this looks posed.', '2002-06-26 19:26:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78375, 2759, 1037, '<td valign="top">Very nicely composed, nice duotone too.</td>', 'Very nicely composed, nice duotone too.', '2002-06-27 02:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78376, 2759, 1, '<td valign="top">This seems very staged, because you wouldn''t normally see someone this clean cut drunk in an alley...  A better subject would''ve produced a better impact.</td>', 'This seems very staged, because you wouldn''t normally see someone this clean cut drunk in an alley...  A better subject would''ve produced a better impact.', '2002-06-27 11:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78377, 2759, 1031, '<td valign="top">I think having restricted aspect ratios might have hurt here. I''d like to see more to create the context of "alley" and not just "doorway". Not a lot more; that''s why I thought a differently-shaped crop might work better...</td>', 'I think having restricted aspect ratios might have hurt here. I''d like to see more to create the context of "alley" and not just "doorway". Not a lot more; that''s why I thought a differently-shaped crop might work better...', '2002-06-27 17:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78378, 2759, 1005, '<td valign="top">Offers a pretty low appreciation for city life.  Photo is well done, but the sadness of the topic makes me want to avoid it.  Sorry.  Photo 8 City 6 total 7</td>', 'Offers a pretty low appreciation for city life.  Photo is well done, but the sadness of the topic makes me want to avoid it.  Sorry.  Photo 8 City 6 total 7', '2002-06-27 18:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78379, 2759, 2448, '<td valign="top">i like this photo</td>', 'i like this photo', '2002-06-27 22:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78380, 2759, 1003, '<td valign="top">sad but true.....</td>', 'sad but true.....', '2002-06-28 11:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78381, 2759, 637, '<td valign="top">Looks less like an alley; more like a closet under construction.  Not clear about connection to challenge.  3 sjgleah</td>', 'Looks less like an alley; more like a closet under construction.  Not clear about connection to challenge.  3 sjgleah', '2002-06-29 18:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78382, 2759, 1054, '<td valign="top">LOL!  Looks a bit posed to me, but I love the idea.</td>', 'LOL!  Looks a bit posed to me, but I love the idea.', '2002-06-30 12:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78383, 2759, 1078, '<td valign="top">Technically a nice picture -- maybe a tad flat, but still pretty nice.  However, I have a hard time believing this isn''t a set picture.  Whether or not the guy is a drunk, he just doesn''t look like he would have fallen asleep in a place like that.  His clothes are too clean, the hat, the sandals, even his beard stubble looks to have been shaved around his neck.  It''s just not believable to me.  Because it has the look of something "photojournalistic" but because I don''t believe it''s a real shot, it loses the impact it might otherwise have.</td>', 'Technically a nice picture -- maybe a tad flat, but still pretty nice.  However, I have a hard time believing this isn''t a set picture.  Whether or not the guy is a drunk, he just doesn''t look like he would have fallen asleep in a place like that.  His clothes are too clean, the hat, the sandals, even his beard stubble looks to have been shaved around his neck.  It''s just not believable to me.  Because it has the look of something "photojournalistic" but because I don''t believe it''s a real shot, it loses the impact it might otherwise have.', '2002-06-30 20:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78384, 2759, 811, '<td valign="top">B/W works well for this I think.  A dirty/holey shirt and pants would''ve really set the mood, too I think.  So, next time, find a drunk, dress him up, dump him in an alley, and take a picture.  :-)</td>', 'B/W works well for this I think.  A dirty/holey shirt and pants would''ve really set the mood, too I think.  So, next time, find a drunk, dress him up, dump him in an alley, and take a picture.  :-)', '2002-06-30 23:07:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78385, 2759, 255, '<td valign="top">wow--shoulda thought a little more about this one before submitting! I wish I had put something about "college" in the title! I didn''t think a thing about it at the time, because I was only seeing it from my perspective--but this is definitely not sad nor is it a homeless person/vagrant type drunk, but one that probably drives a BMW and lives in a Frat house! This is so common here--we get bombarded by thousands of college kids (Chapel Hill, etc.) every summer who pretty much take over! It has gotten so bad that the cops think they need reinforcements--the kind that dress in all black and hide in the bushes--to "keep the residents safe". That sucks, but people do get mad at these kids for passing out on their porches, in their lawn furniture, etc. I even found a guy under my car one night! Pretty bizarre, especially when you think of these guys as our future politicians/lawers/doctors! Anyway, considering that they drink practically non-stop all weekend, it isn''t really surprising--it''s really pretty funny when you see it all the time--and it isn''t sad because their friends are usually close by. We told the bouncer at the bar about this guy--so I''m sure he was fine!</td>', 'wow--shoulda thought a little more about this one before submitting! I wish I had put something about "college" in the title! I didn''t think a thing about it at the time, because I was only seeing it from my perspective--but this is definitely not sad nor is it a homeless person/vagrant type drunk, but one that probably drives a BMW and lives in a Frat house! This is so common here--we get bombarded by thousands of college kids (Chapel Hill, etc.) every summer who pretty much take over! It has gotten so bad that the cops think they need reinforcements--the kind that dress in all black and hide in the bushes--to "keep the residents safe". That sucks, but people do get mad at these kids for passing out on their porches, in their lawn furniture, etc. I even found a guy under my car one night! Pretty bizarre, especially when you think of these guys as our future politicians/lawers/doctors! Anyway, considering that they drink practically non-stop all weekend, it isn''t really surprising--it''s really pretty funny when you see it all the time--and it isn''t sad because their friends are usually close by. We told the bouncer at the bar about this guy--so I''m sure he was fine!', '2002-07-01 01:13:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(78386, 2759, 1078, '<td valign="top">While I wasn''t the only one to think it was staged, nevertheless, I still have to say my bad.  :-)<br/><br/>I like knowing the backstory.  It makes me regret the comments I made because it is a good photojournalist style shot -- I just had my mind set on a completely different stereo-type.</td>', 'While I wasn''t the only one to think it was staged, nevertheless, I still have to say my bad.  :-)I like knowing the backstory.  It makes me regret the comments I made because it is a good photojournalist style shot -- I just had my mind set on a completely different stereo-type.', '2002-07-01 02:36:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(78387, 2759, 1005, '<td valign="top">With the background story, I can better relate!  I sort of remember this kind of evening, college years are still a bit hazy.....Thanks for the explanation.  This really is a great example of photojournalism.</td>', 'With the background story, I can better relate!  I sort of remember this kind of evening, college years are still a bit hazy.....Thanks for the explanation.  This really is a great example of photojournalism.', '2002-07-01 17:32:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(78388, 2759, 449, '<td valign="top">I know the window he is sitting in, the old brick building down on the river. So the Ice House is still up and running huh? I thought it was sold. Glad to see the downtown life is still how I remember it. I think I may have been on that ledge a time or two. How was the reggae? Miss you. Les</td>', 'I know the window he is sitting in, the old brick building down on the river. So the Ice House is still up and running huh? I thought it was sold. Glad to see the downtown life is still how I remember it. I think I may have been on that ledge a time or two. How was the reggae? Miss you. Les', '2002-07-02 00:55:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(78389, 2759, 255, '<td valign="top">Hi Les of the Great White North!! Good to hear from ya! I didn''t stick around for the reggae for this shot, way  too chaotic.<br/>Also, I think you are thinking about the alley above Blue Post...this one is right behind the Ice House, and it is a doorway the poor sap has taken over--<br/>notice the weeds!:)</td>', 'Hi Les of the Great White North!! Good to hear from ya! I didn''t stick around for the reggae for this shot, way  too chaotic.Also, I think you are thinking about the alley above Blue Post...this one is right behind the Ice House, and it is a doorway the poor sap has taken over--notice the weeds!:)', '2002-07-02 15:56:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(78390, 2760, 772, '<td valign="top">I really like the quality of this photo and the concept provided by it, but I''m not really buying into this particular image as a ''city life'' photo... = 5 - jmsetzler</td>', 'I really like the quality of this photo and the concept provided by it, but I''m not really buying into this particular image as a ''city life'' photo... = 5 - jmsetzler', '2002-06-24 03:06:00.000000', NULL, 1),
