(78450, 2762, 1005, '<td valign="top">How did you blow out the sky so completely?  I like the yellow on the horizon and the coloration of the buildings.  Photo 6 City 8 total 7</td>', 'How did you blow out the sky so completely?  I like the yellow on the horizon and the coloration of the buildings.  Photo 6 City 8 total 7', '2002-06-27 16:06:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78451, 2762, 772, '<td valign="top">This is a phenomenal photo... This is definitely worthy of a ribbon this week.  I LOVE the way the sunlight is reflecting off the sides of the buildings and the car windows.  The composition of this photo is excellent and you have a great eye to have noticed this opportunity.  It seems like you may have intentionally under exposed this one a bit... Good move!  Great shot... kudos :) = 10 - jmsetzler</td>', 'This is a phenomenal photo... This is definitely worthy of a ribbon this week.  I LOVE the way the sunlight is reflecting off the sides of the buildings and the car windows.  The composition of this photo is excellent and you have a great eye to have noticed this opportunity.  It seems like you may have intentionally under exposed this one a bit... Good move!  Great shot... kudos :) = 10 - jmsetzler', '2002-06-28 12:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78452, 2762, 2343, '<td valign="top">Your composition and depth are excellent as well as the clarity on the buildings.  Great job!</td>', 'Your composition and depth are excellent as well as the clarity on the buildings.  Great job!', '2002-06-29 01:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78453, 2762, 715, '<td valign="top">Outstanding colors and great composition! Without any doubt my favorite for this week.</td>', 'Outstanding colors and great composition! Without any doubt my favorite for this week.', '2002-06-29 11:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78454, 2762, 1054, '<td valign="top">Excellent execution!</td>', 'Excellent execution!', '2002-06-29 22:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78455, 2762, 1, '<td valign="top">Wow.  Awesome framing... the lighting is unbelievable.  The driving car is a perfect touch.</td>', 'Wow.  Awesome framing... the lighting is unbelievable.  The driving car is a perfect touch.', '2002-06-30 17:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78456, 2762, 2221, '<td valign="top">Great photo! I like the lighting very much and the soft, warm color. The driving car is pressed a litte too close on the left side. More space there would be nice but I guess there were other cars parking on this side which you better cropped out.<br/>Photo 9, Creativity 9, City Life 9 = 9</td>', 'Great photo! I like the lighting very much and the soft, warm color. The driving car is pressed a litte too close on the left side. More space there would be nice but I guess there were other cars parking on this side which you better cropped out.Photo 9, Creativity 9, City Life 9 = 9', '2002-06-30 20:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78457, 2762, 308, '<td valign="top">Beautiful!  I love the colors and I love the cropping.</td>', 'Beautiful!  I love the colors and I love the cropping.', '2002-06-30 20:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78458, 2762, 527, '<td valign="top">I would like to see the image composed with more road and a little more room to the left of the car. The colors are working well.<br/><br/>7  -Tim</td>', 'I would like to see the image composed with more road and a little more room to the left of the car. The colors are working well.7  -Tim', '2002-06-30 23:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78459, 2762, 2, '<td valign="top">This is a marvelous shot... congrats on your high placement.  I can''t wait to see your future submissions.</td>', 'This is a marvelous shot... congrats on your high placement.  I can''t wait to see your future submissions.', '2002-07-01 01:06:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(78460, 2762, 693, '<td valign="top">This should have placed higher.  Really great photo!<br/><br/>Nice camera by the way :-)</td>', 'This should have placed higher.  Really great photo!Nice camera by the way :-)', '2002-07-01 13:18:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(78461, 2762, 2244, '<td valign="top">I wanted to thank everyone for your kind comments.<br/><br/>It''s interesting to see how people prefer the picture with or without the car, with more or less road etc....  I tend to be very instinctive...I always, always look for shots, no matter what I do, whether I have a camera or not.  I always regret those I don''t shoot.  The real exceptional thing about this city shot was that there were no cars on the street for about 1 minute, which is really rare, especially at this time of day in NYC.<br/><br/>As far as the "development" is concerned, the only thing I changed from the original was straightening the horizon (i.e. rotating the photo slightly), which means that I effectively had to crop about 3% of the border all around.  I also added a little contrast and saturation from the original using "Levels" in Photoshop.  All in all it''s very close to how I got it on camera!<br/><br/>Good luck to everyone on the coming challenges!</td>', 'I wanted to thank everyone for your kind comments.It''s interesting to see how people prefer the picture with or without the car, with more or less road etc....  I tend to be very instinctive...I always, always look for shots, no matter what I do, whether I have a camera or not.  I always regret those I don''t shoot.  The real exceptional thing about this city shot was that there were no cars on the street for about 1 minute, which is really rare, especially at this time of day in NYC.As far as the "development" is concerned, the only thing I changed from the original was straightening the horizon (i.e. rotating the photo slightly), which means that I effectively had to crop about 3% of the border all around.  I also added a little contrast and saturation from the original using "Levels" in Photoshop.  All in all it''s very close to how I got it on camera!Good luck to everyone on the coming challenges!', '2002-07-09 13:46:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(78462, 2765, 693, '<td valign="top">The drivers side view mirror doesn''t belong in the frame and thus should have been cropped out.</td>', 'The drivers side view mirror doesn''t belong in the frame and thus should have been cropped out.', '2002-06-24 01:51:00.000000', NULL, 1),
