(77363, 2705, 527, '<td valign="top">This is great! Maybe the only thing I would change would be to have lowered the point of view just a little to eliminate the line on the top right and to include the feet of the feet of the people in the foreground. I would probably have to see it to know for sure.<br/><br/>9  -Tim</td>', 'This is great! Maybe the only thing I would change would be to have lowered the point of view just a little to eliminate the line on the top right and to include the feet of the feet of the people in the foreground. I would probably have to see it to know for sure.9  -Tim', '2002-06-30 23:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(77364, 2705, 772, '<td valign="top">Bruno, congrats on second place :)  Good shot !</td>', 'Bruno, congrats on second place :)  Good shot !', '2002-07-01 02:50:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(77365, 2705, 1796, '<td valign="top">thank you all for the great comments and scores! I''m almost glad I didn''t win  -  there wouldn''t be much chance of improvement that way  ;-) actually, it''s probably all down from here anyway...<br/>I took the shot during a nice dinner at Metrazur, the restaurant on the East Balcony. It''s a truly splendid way to combine a hobby with a "buzzing meal". For those of you who''ve never been to NYC, GCT is definitely a place to go when you do get here, dinner of course optional. This terminal''s cathedral-like hall, the buzz and mumbling of the crowd (I''d say it doesn''t even get loud during rush hour), the light, the masses pouring out into the hall from arriving commuter trains  -  simply beautiful.<br/>The picture was taken using the ballustrade as a tripod substitute, which might explain the little  tilt and the camera was set to automatic, no flash of course. My camera doesn''t have any manual settings apart from white balance and exposure correction and I measured the light in different places till I got the picture I wanted instead of playing with exposure bias values.<br/><br/>It''s all FEAR from here... good luck everyone!</td>', 'thank you all for the great comments and scores! I''m almost glad I didn''t win  -  there wouldn''t be much chance of improvement that way  ;-) actually, it''s probably all down from here anyway...I took the shot during a nice dinner at Metrazur, the restaurant on the East Balcony. It''s a truly splendid way to combine a hobby with a "buzzing meal". For those of you who''ve never been to NYC, GCT is definitely a place to go when you do get here, dinner of course optional. This terminal''s cathedral-like hall, the buzz and mumbling of the crowd (I''d say it doesn''t even get loud during rush hour), the light, the masses pouring out into the hall from arriving commuter trains  -  simply beautiful.The picture was taken using the ballustrade as a tripod substitute, which might explain the little  tilt and the camera was set to automatic, no flash of course. My camera doesn''t have any manual settings apart from white balance and exposure correction and I measured the light in different places till I got the picture I wanted instead of playing with exposure bias values.It''s all FEAR from here... good luck everyone!', '2002-07-01 08:33:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(77366, 2705, 1569, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!!!!!! Exellent pix!!!!</td>', 'Congratulations!!!!!! Exellent pix!!!!', '2002-07-01 08:44:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(77367, 2705, 1907, '<td valign="top">Yes, it reminds me of the Baraka scene too... where the people travelling through a train station are compared to chickens in a batch line</td>', 'Yes, it reminds me of the Baraka scene too... where the people travelling through a train station are compared to chickens in a batch line', '2002-07-02 03:44:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(77368, 2706, 885, '<td valign="top">If you could, I might have cropped down to include a portion of the tree and building, but emphasize the crane a little more</td>', 'If you could, I might have cropped down to include a portion of the tree and building, but emphasize the crane a little more', '2002-06-24 09:55:00.000000', NULL, 1);
.  <br/><br/><br/></td>', 'Well it took a few months but I finally did it!! Thank you all so much for enjoying and voting for my picture.  It took along time to get this shot right; I posted some of my outtakes here.   Some thought that I used rear sync flash but in actuality I used the natural lighting, and shot next to a stop sign so the car stopped just long enough to burn in a ghost image, and the rest was up to the 5 second exposure.  I used the hood of someones car as a tripod since I forgot to bring mine, and as every photographer knows improvisation can be your best friend.  Any way congrats to everyone who submitted an image, I believe we are all winners because we each share a common love for photography and the joy it brings each of us.  ', '2002-07-01 01:42:00.000000', NULL, 0),
